Dependencies built into the binary
----------------------------------

syntect (https://github.com/trishume/syntect), the code highlighter — MIT; two-face
(https://codeberg.org/CosmicHarper/two-face), the grammars it reads — MIT OR Apache-2.0. The
grammars come from the bat project, each under its own licence (MIT or Apache-2.0): their texts
are in NOTICE-grammars.md.

The other Rust crates (listed in Cargo.lock) are under permissive licences: MIT, Apache-2.0,
BSD, ISC, Zlib or Unicode-3.0; `cargo deny check licenses` verifies it (deny.toml).

Programs used, not included
---------------------------

The diagrams are rendered by programs of the user's machine, which glitu runs and does not
include: skemo (https://skemo.net, MIT OR Apache-2.0), Graphviz, D2, mermaid-cli. For the
mermaid.chromium engine, glitu downloads mermaid.js (https://github.com/mermaid-js/mermaid, MIT
license), a pinned version checked by its SHA-256, into the user's cache.
